# INVWINWB.KEY - a key script of INVWIN, as INVWIN.KEY: a location's
# contents, all items or those not installed in another, its own or
# those of every location below it too.  Item 1 is installed into item
# 3, both then at Shelf A1.  The contents of Shelf A1, which holds Box
# B2, open with the items of both, the title ending "(all items,
# everything below)"; Record > Not installed only (ALT-C Y), which is
# then checked, leaves out item 1, the title saying "not installed"; the
# entry chosen again brings it back and unchecks the entry.  The mode is
# kept through Esc back from item 3's parts, a scoped list opened from
# the contents; Record > Everything below (ALT-C G) then leaves Shelf
# A1's own items.  Leaving the contents in both modes, a location opened next
# starts afresh: Shelf A1 again with everything below it, Box B2 with
# its own items.  The end by Exit.
# TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/INVWINWB.SNP is its snapshot.
T ADMIN
K TAB
T Retro1986
K ENTER
S ITEMS
K ALT-C I
T 3
K ENTER
S INSTLD
K ALT-L B
S LOCS
K DOWN ENTER
S ALL
K ALT-C
S ALLMENU
K ESC ESC ALT-C Y
S TOP
K ALT-C
S TOPMENU
K ESC ESC ALT-C Y
S ALLAGN
K ALT-C
S ALLMEN2
K ESC ESC
# the menu entry toggles both ways
K ALT-C Y
S MTOP
K ALT-C Y
S MALL
# not installed again, then a scoped list from the contents and back
K ALT-C Y ALT-C P
S PARTS
K ESC
S KEPT
K ALT-C G
S HERE
# a location's contents start afresh: Shelf A1 opened again after the
# modes were changed, and Box B2
K ESC ENTER
S A1ALL
K ESC DOWN ENTER
S B2
K ESC ESC
K ALT-F X
